      "name": "ochre",
      "symbol": "o",
      "recipe": "Iron oxide earth roasted to a red-brown. Grind fine on a stone, then temper with hide glue until it flows like cream; two coats read as one solid field."
    },
    {
      "name": "azurite",
      "symbol": "a",
      "recipe": "Azurite ground coarse and washed three times to throw off the pale green. Bind with hide glue; keep the wash thin so the rawhide stays supple."
    },
    {
      "name": "charcoal",
      "symbol": "k",
      "recipe": "Willow charcoal milled to a soft black. Sift through muslin to drop the grit, then mix with a little glue and a drop of ox gall so it wets out."
    },
    {
      "name": "bone white",
      "symbol": "w",
      "recipe": "Calcined bone, slaked and ground to a chalky white. Lay it on last and thick, since it will not cover over a dark earth once that has dried."
    }
  ],
